==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|skemtiligr||amusing, interesting, pleasant}}, confer the Old Norse {{m|non|óskemtiligr||dull, uninteresting}}, {{m|non|skemtiliga||amusingly, pleasantly}}, {{m|non|skemta||to amuse, to entertain}}, {{m|non|skemtan}} or {{m|non|skemtun||entertainment}} and {{m|non|skemtanligr||amusing, pleasant}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈscɛm̥tɪˌlɛːɣʏr/|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|skemmtilegri|skemmtilegastur}}

# [[funny]], [[amusing]]{{jump|is|funny|s}}
#: ''Systir hans þykir '''skemmtileg'''.''
#:: His sister is considered to be '''amusing'''.
# [[entertaining]], [[diverting]]{{jump|is|entertaining|s}}
# [[interesting]]{{jump|is|interesting|s}}

